        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Blend the fish, garlic, {{fish-sauce}}, {{cornflour}}, egg, {{caster-sugar}}, and chilli flakes in a food processor until completely smooth."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Transfer to a bowl and fold in the shredded kaffir lime leaves. Cover and refrigerate for 30 minutes to firm the paste."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Shape into 12 round patties about 1.5 cm thick using damp hands."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oil in a wide frying pan over medium-high heat. Fry the patties in batches for 3 minutes per side until golden and cooked through."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Drain on kitchen paper. Serve hot with lime wedges and a ready-made sweet chilli dipping sauce."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Patties are falling apart in the pan",
              "cause": "Fish paste was not smooth enough or not chilled",
              "fix": "Blend until silky smooth with no chunks. Return to the fridge for a further 20 minutes before shaping."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Outside is dark but inside is still raw",
              "cause": "Pan too hot and patties too thick",
              "fix": "Keep patties to 1.5 cm thickness and cook at medium rather than high heat."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Cakes are very dense and rubbery",
              "cause": "Over-processed or too much cornflour",
              "fix": "Blend just until smooth. Use the exact quantity of cornflour specified."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tod man pla is sold from street carts and market stalls across Thailand. The name means fried fish cake. The bouncy texture that distinguishes it from Western fish cakes comes from beating the fish into a smooth paste. This develops the protein in the fish in a way that gives the cooked cake its characteristic springiness. Kaffir lime leaves are essential. No other herb gives the same combination of fragrance and texture when shredded into the paste."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
